{"base_rate":0.29515418502202645,"brier":0.1864876651982379,"bss":0.1035892817164179,"bss_hi":0.19323897376085233,"bss_lo":-0.023974443936046717,"chart":{"base":[444.7,72.3],"fp":[210.3,265.1],"lead":"62,297.2 272,301.3 482,298.9 692,300.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.10 — higher than 17% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.7 °C — better than 98% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 6%; promised 88% → rained 62%"},"rel":"80,440.8 164.2,414.5 296,365.1 439.6,280.4 617.1,196.8"},"country":"CW","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12997063142437593,"ess":401.32224038033013,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Willemstad</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Willemstad rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>72%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 681 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 12.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.10, ranked 176 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(150&ndash;189) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>31</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>89</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></