 range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"98.88268292682926\" cy=\"337.609756097561\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 22%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"135.05913043478262\" cy=\"339.7971014492754\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"168.61138461538465\" cy=\"314.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 42%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"208.35166666666666\" cy=\"280.8888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"249.5764705882353\" cy=\"237.47058823529412\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 66%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"291.05880597014925\" cy=\"213.5820895522388\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 81%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"343.0982608695652\" cy=\"192.08695652173913\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 72% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.7113043478262\" cy=\"118.231884057971\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Willemstad the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.28) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.16).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>150</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>-0.161</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>-0.002</td><td class='num'>17.9%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.104</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.282</td><td class='num'>4.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":12.12246,"lon":-68.88641,"n":681,"n_cities":213,"name":"Willemstad","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":31,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.038539325842696634,